%description:

The power a transmission is recorded at on the radio medium: the power its
frame is sent at.

A UE's frame carries two powers in its control information, the cellular
transmit power and the D2D one. Every interference computation takes an
interfering transmission's power from its record on the medium, so the
transmitter has to record the power the frame is really sent at: the
cellular power for an uplink frame, the D2D power for a D2D frame, one-to-one
and one-to-many alike.

Checked with one UE's control information carrying 23 dBm cellular and
15 dBm D2D power, through the transmitter, for an uplink, a one-to-one D2D
and a one-to-many D2D data frame.

%includes:
#include <string>
#include <memory>
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/radio/CellularTransmitter.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/radio/RadioTransmissionRequest.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.stack.phy.radio.CellularTransmitter;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        transmitter: CellularTransmitter;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *transmitter = harnessModule<CellularTransmitter>(this, "transmitter");

StubEndpoint ue;
ue.nodeId = MacNodeId(1025);
ue.coord = inet::Coord(100, 20, 1.5);

RadioTransmissionRequest request;
request.sender = &ue;
request.cellId = MacNodeId(1);
request.duration = SimTime(1, SIMTIME_MS);

// the power the transmitter records for a data frame of the UE in the given direction
auto recordedPower = [&] (Direction dir) {
    UserControlInfo info;
    info.setSourceId(ue.nodeId);
    info.setDestId(MacNodeId(1026));
    info.setDirection(dir);
    info.setFrameType(DATAPKT);
    info.setTxPower(23.0);
    info.setD2dTxPower(15.0);
    std::unique_ptr<CellularTransmission> transmission(transmitter->createTransmission(request, info));
    return transmission->txPower;
};

double ul = recordedPower(UL), d2d = recordedPower(D2D), d2dMulti = recordedPower(D2D_MULTI);
c.check("an uplink frame is recorded at the cellular power", ul == 23.0, std::to_string(ul));
c.check("a one-to-one D2D frame is recorded at the D2D power", d2d == 15.0, std::to_string(d2d));
c.check("a one-to-many D2D frame is recorded at the D2D power", d2dMulti == 15.0, std::to_string(d2dMulti));

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=3 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
